        {
          "id": 1934441,
          "username": "hizachlee",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/hizachlee/{size}/416069_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-08T03:14:07.816Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Shopify only charges a flat shipping rate once across two locations when both locations sit in the same location group inside one shipping profile and use flat or price-based rates.</p>\n<p>If your shipping profile uses weight-based or carrier-calculated rates, or if the two stores are in separate location groups under Settings &gt; Shipping and delivery, Shopify calculates a rate for each origin location and adds them together at checkout.</p>",
          "post_number": 2,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 6,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-08T03:14:07.816Z",
          "reply_count": 1,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "incoming_link_count": 0,
          "reads": 6,
          "readers_count": 5,
          "score": 6.2,
          "yours": false,
          "topic_id": 711715,
          "topic_slug": "two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment",
