        {
          "id": 1934449,
          "username": "Shawn-Z",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-11-08T03:41:59.738Z",
          "cooked": "<p>Put both stores in the same location group and use a flat or price-based rate, and the double charge goes away. Right now your customers are being charged for two shipments because the two locations sit in separate location groups, so Shopify adds each location’s rate together instead of charging one. It’s a rate configuration problem, not a packing one, since checkout runs before you combine the stock.</p>\n<p>Go to Settings &gt; Shipping and delivery, open the shipping profile that covers these products, then Fulfillment locations, click the second store, choose “Use existing shipping options from another location”, pick the first store and save. Both locations are then in one group and the rate is charged once.</p>\n<p>Watch the rate name too, since rates with the same name are added together at checkout even across profiles. One limit: if the rate is weight-based or carrier-calculated, this won’t produce a single charge for an order fulfilled from two locations, because those are calculated per product and the results are combined.</p>",
          "post_number": 3,
          "post_type": 1,
          "posts_count": 6,
          "updated_at": "2026-11-08T03:41:59.738Z",
          "reply_count": 1,
          "reply_to_post_number": null,
