    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1877894,
      "summarized_text": "A retailer with two nearby stores combines stock and ships customer orders as one parcel, but checkout has recently charged customers for shipping from both locations. The suggested fix of placing both stores in the same location group works for flat or price-based rates; it does not prevent multiple charges with weight-based or carrier-calculated rates, which Shopify calculates separately for each fulfillment location and combines.\n\nThe retailer confirmed that its shipping rates are weight-based, so the location-group change will not solve the problem. The latest suggestion is to disable “available to fulfill online orders” for the second store, so checkout uses only the first store as an origin and charges one rate. However, this means online orders can use only the first store’s stock, limiting the ability to fulfill from or combine inventory at the second store. No solution was confirmed that preserves both locations’ online inventory while charging a single weight-based shipping rate, so the issue remains unresolved.",
      "algorithm": "gpt-6-luna",
      "outdated": false,
