  "comments": [
    {
      "author": "hizachlee",
      "text": "Shopify only charges a flat shipping rate once across two locations when both locations sit in the same location group inside one shipping profile and use flat or price-based rates. \n If your shipping profile uses weight-based or carrier-calculated rates, or if the two stores are in separate location groups under Settings > Shipping and delivery, Shopify calculates a rate for each origin location and adds them together at checkout.",
      "at": "2026-11-08T03:14:07.816Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment/711715/2"
    },
    {
      "author": "Shawn-Z",
      "text": "Put both stores in the same location group and use a flat or price-based rate, and the double charge goes away. Right now your customers are being charged for two shipments because the two locations sit in separate location groups, so Shopify adds each location’s rate together instead of charging one. It’s a rate configuration problem, not a packing one, since checkout runs before you combine the stock. \n Go to Settings > Shipping and delivery, open the shipping profile that covers these products, then Fulfillment locations, click the second store, choose “Use existing shipping options from another location”, pick the first store and save. Both locations are then in one group and the rate is charged once. \n Watch the rate name too, since rates with the same name are added together at checkout even across profiles. One limit: if the rate is weight-based or carrier-calculated, this won’t produce a single charge for an order fulfilled from two locations, because those are calculated per product and the results are combined.",
      "at": "2026-11-08T03:41:59.738Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment/711715/3"
    },
    {
      "author": "TVR_UK",
      "text": "Unfortunately our shipping is weight based.",
      "at": "2026-11-08T06:32:55.364Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment/711715/4"
    },
    {
      "author": "TVR_UK",
      "text": "Unfortunately our shipping is weight based, so not working for us.",
      "at": "2026-11-08T06:34:01.881Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment/711715/5"
    },
    {
      "author": "hizachlee",
      "text": "With weight-based rates, Shopify adds a rate for each location. Turn off “available to fulfill online orders” on the second store, so checkout sees one origin and charges once. Online orders then only use the first store’s stock.",
      "at": "2026-11-08T06:52:26.907Z",
      "url": "https://community.shopify.com/t/two-locations-shared-inventory-one-shipment/711715/6"
    }
  ],
